      "title": "Unrelated new construction can lose its inverse lot link",
      "basis": "Source-derived concrete case, not reproduced by a new critic browser run.",
      "detail": "A lot that has the same key/ID before and after the road action is outside changedLotIds. If it was free in zoningBefore but has since gained a building, undo deserializes its saved buildingId:null. Buildings.restoreTransaction preserves that unrelated building object but never rebinds the unchanged live lot. The existing level-change fixture cannot detect this.",
      "next": "Preserve current owner links on unaffected same-key/same-ID lots and test a free-to-built unrelated lot through undo and redo with both inverse directions."
    },
