      "rank": 2,
      "severity": "medium",
      "owner": "Tools / history",
      "title": "Failure atomicity is bounded to a settled one-shot rejection",
      "basis": "Source path and verification coverage.",
      "detail": "restoreOwners captures rollback without settling pending Zoning. An immediate undo plus late rejection can capture a current graph and stale lot table. rollbackOwners may itself fail/throw; current code only logs or propagates and leaves no recoverable compensation journal. The tested rejection returns false once before Zoning mutation and succeeds on compensation.",
      "next": "Settle a coherent rollback pre-image and retain a recovery policy when compensation fails; add immediate undo plus one-shot failure coverage."
    },
